WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.368 --> 00:00:01.910
MARK MIRCHANDANI:
Today we're talking

00:00:01.910 --> 00:00:04.250
about database auditing,
multicloud fluency,

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.930
and enhanced customer
experience management.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.990
I'm Mark and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:12.461
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:12.461 --> 00:00:15.490
If you manage sensitive
data in your MySQL database,

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:17.820
you might be obligated
to record and monitor

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.860
user database activity,
especially if you

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.630
work in a regulated industry.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:24.900
Cloud SQL for MySQL has
developed a new audit plugin

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.750
called the Cloud SQL for
MySQL Audit Plugin that

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.730
offers enterprise-grade
database auditing

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.759
to help you maintain a strong
compliance security posture.

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:34.770
You can now define audit
rules that govern which

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:37.800
database activity is recorded.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.978
As IT footprints
get more complex,

00:00:39.978 --> 00:00:42.270
you can expect to see a
broader range of cloud provider

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.910
requirements showing up
where you work and interview,

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:47.350
ready or not,
multicloud is happening.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:49.830
And while multicloud fluency
is a huge opportunity

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:52.290
for an engineer, how do you
make the most of your time

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.480
and bandwidth to meet that goal?

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.330
Check out the blog for thoughts
on gaining multicloud fluency

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:00.140
and where to focus.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.170
Sprinklr, the unified customer
experience management platform

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:05.870
for modern enterprises, has
partnered with Google Cloud

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:07.700
to accelerate its
go-to-market strategy

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.535
and grow awareness among
our joint customers.

00:01:10.535 --> 00:01:12.410
To learn more about this
exciting partnership

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.780
and the challenges we
jointly solve for customers,

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.850
check out the recent
conversation between Google

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:20.330
Cloud's VP of marketing,
Sarah Kennedy, and Sprinklr's

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.490
chief experience
officer, Grad Conn,

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:25.640
or read the press release
on the partnership.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:27.230
The cloud can be
complicated, which

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:29.272
is why we've been working
on helping Google Cloud

00:01:29.272 --> 00:01:30.770
users with Active Assist.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:33.410
It's a portfolio of tools to
help you optimize your cloud

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:36.020
usage and configuration,
with recommendations

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:38.030
around cost,
performance, security,

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.692
and even sustainability.

00:01:39.692 --> 00:01:41.150
Check out the new
product page that

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:44.187
helps break down which solutions
you can get started with.

00:01:44.187 --> 00:01:46.270
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:48.520
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:51.320
Any thoughts or ideas, leave
us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.850
We'll see you in the cloud.

